{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Miyr1m1D3nP7fiHku5aEye","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd088-encutil\n2\ttitle: \"pkg/encutil: Shared Encoding and Decoding Library\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Three cmd/ utilities (base32, base64, basenc) share identical logic for encoding stdin\n6\t  or file input, decoding with whitespace and garbage tolerance, and wrapping output at\n7\t  a configurable column width. Without a shared package, each utility reimplements the\n8\t  read-encode-wrap-write pipeline and the decode-ignore-garbage pipeline.\n9\t\n10\t  pkg/encutil provides the shared encoding/decoding pipeline. Each cmd/ utility imports\n11\t  this package and supplies the encoding scheme; all I/O, wrapping, and error handling\n12\t  is delegated to pkg/encutil.\n13\t\n14\tgoals:\n15\t  - G1: Provide a generic encode pipeline that reads input, encodes it, and writes wrapped output.\n16\t  - G2: Provide a generic decode pipeline that reads encoded input, optionally ignores garbage, and writes decoded output.\n17\t  - G3: Support configurable wrap width and encoding schemes.\n18\t\n19\trequirements:\n20\t  R1:\n21\t    title: Encoding pipeline\n22\t    items:\n23\t      - R1.1:\n24\t          text: |\n25\t            Must provide an EncoderConfig struct:\n26\t\n27\t              type EncoderConfig struct {\n28\t                  Encode   func(src []byte) string  // encoding function\n29\t                  WrapCol  int                       // wrap column (0 = no wrap, default 76)\n30\t              }\n31\t      - R1.2:\n32\t          text: Must provide func Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error that reads all input from r, encodes it using cfg.Encode, wraps the output at cfg.WrapCol characters per line, and writes to w.\n33\t      - R1.3:\n34\t          text: When WrapCol is 0, must write the entire encoded output as a single line followed by a newline.\n35\t\n36\t  R2:\n37\t    title: Decoding pipeline\n38\t    items:\n39\t      - R2.1:\n40\t          text: |\n41\t            Must provide a DecoderConfig struct:\n42\t\n43\t              type DecoderConfig struct {\n44\t                  Decode        func(src string) ([]byte, error) // decoding function\n45\t                  IgnoreGarbage bool                              // ignore non-alphabet characters\n46\t              }\n47\t      - R2.2:\n48\t          text: Must provide func Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error that reads all encoded input from r, strips whitespace, optionally strips non-alphabet characters (when IgnoreGarbage is true), decodes, and writes the binary result to w.\n49\t      - R2.3:\n50\t          text: Must return an error when the input contains invalid characters and IgnoreGarbage is false.\n51\t\n52\t  R3:\n53\t    title: File handling\n54\t    items:\n55\t      - R3.1:\n56\t          text: Must provide func OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error) that opens the named file, or returns os.Stdin when filename is empty or \"-\".\n57\t      - R3.2:\n58\t          text: Must exit 1 when the input file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr.\n59\t\n60\tnon_goals:\n61\t  - pkg/encutil does not implement any specific encoding scheme; callers provide encode/decode functions.\n62\t  - pkg/encutil does not handle SIGPIPE; each cmd/ utility calls pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler independently.\n63\t\n64\tpackage_contract:\n65\t  exports:\n66\t    - name: EncoderConfig\n67\t      signature: \"type EncoderConfig struct { Encode func([]byte) string; WrapCol int }\"\n68\t    - name: DecoderConfig\n69\t      signature: \"type DecoderConfig struct { Decode func(string) ([]byte, error); IgnoreGarbage bool }\"\n70\t    - name: Encode\n71\t      signature: \"func Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error\"\n72\t    - name: Decode\n73\t      signature: \"func Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error\"\n74\t    - name: OpenInput\n75\t      signature: \"func OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error)\"\n76\t  imports:\n77\t    - io\n78\t    - os\n79\t    - bufio\n80\t    - strings\n81\t  import_constraints:\n82\t    - \"Must not import any cmd/ package.\"\n83\t    - \"Must not import any other pkg/ package.\"\n84\t\n85\tacceptance_criteria:\n86\t  - id: AC1\n87\t    criterion: \"Encode with Base64 encoder wraps at 76 characters by default.\"\n88\t    traces:\n89\t      - R1.1\n90\t      - R1.2\n91\t      - R1.3\n92\t  - id: AC2\n93\t    criterion: \"Encode with WrapCol=0 produces single-line output.\"\n94\t    traces:\n95\t      - R1.3\n96\t  - id: AC3\n97\t    criterion: \"Decode with Base64 decoder and IgnoreGarbage=true ignores non-alphabet characters.\"\n98\t    traces:\n99\t      - R2.1\n100\t      - R2.2\n101\t      - R2.3\n102\t  - id: AC4\n103\t    criterion: \"Decode with IgnoreGarbage=false returns error on invalid input.\"\n104\t    traces:\n105\t      - R2.3\n106\t  - id: AC5\n107\t    criterion: \"OpenInput('-') returns os.Stdin.\"\n108\t    traces:\n109\t      - R3.1\n110\t  - id: AC6\n111\t    criterion: \"pkg/encutil compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n112\t    traces:\n113\t      - R1.1\n114\t      - R1.2\n115\t      - R1.3\n116\t      - R2.1\n117\t      - R2.2\n118\t      - R2.3\n119\t      - R3.1\n120\t      - R3.2\n121\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4fc28f23-4d8c-4641-908e-5e9d69890c03","uuid":"b2f90b4d-25d9-45c5-9aa9-531d9a765e7e","timestamp":"2026-05-13T23:44:28.770Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5097/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd088-encutil.yaml","content":"id: srd088-encutil\ntitle: \"pkg/encutil: Shared Encoding and Decoding Library\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Three cmd/ utilities (base32, base64, basenc) share identical logic for encoding stdin\n  or file input, decoding with whitespace and garbage tolerance, and wrapping output at\n  a configurable column width. Without a shared package, each utility reimplements the\n  read-encode-wrap-write pipeline and the decode-ignore-garbage pipeline.\n\n  pkg/encutil provides the shared encoding/decoding pipeline. Each cmd/ utility imports\n  this package and supplies the encoding scheme; all I/O, wrapping, and error handling\n  is delegated to pkg/encutil.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Provide a generic encode pipeline that reads input, encodes it, and writes wrapped output.\n  - G2: Provide a generic decode pipeline that reads encoded input, optionally ignores garbage, and writes decoded output.\n  - G3: Support configurable wrap width and encoding schemes.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Encoding pipeline\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: |\n            Must provide an EncoderConfig struct:\n\n              type EncoderConfig struct {\n                  Encode   func(src []byte) string  // encoding function\n                  WrapCol  int                       // wrap column (0 = no wrap, default 76)\n              }\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must provide func Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error that reads all input from r, encodes it using cfg.Encode, wraps the output at cfg.WrapCol characters per line, and writes to w.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: When WrapCol is 0, must write the entire encoded output as a single line followed by a newline.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Decoding pipeline\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: |\n            Must provide a DecoderConfig struct:\n\n              type DecoderConfig struct {\n                  Decode        func(src string) ([]byte, error) // decoding function\n                  IgnoreGarbage bool                              // ignore non-alphabet characters\n              }\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must provide func Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error that reads all encoded input from r, strips whitespace, optionally strips non-alphabet characters (when IgnoreGarbage is true), decodes, and writes the binary result to w.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must return an error when the input contains invalid characters and IgnoreGarbage is false.\n\n  R3:\n    title: File handling\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must provide func OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error) that opens the named file, or returns os.Stdin when filename is empty or \"-\".\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when the input file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - pkg/encutil does not implement any specific encoding scheme; callers provide encode/decode functions.\n  - pkg/encutil does not handle SIGPIPE; each cmd/ utility calls pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler independently.\n\npackage_contract:\n  exports:\n    - name: EncoderConfig\n      signature: \"type EncoderConfig struct { Encode func([]byte) string; WrapCol int }\"\n    - name: DecoderConfig\n      signature: \"type DecoderConfig struct { Decode func(string) ([]byte, error); IgnoreGarbage bool }\"\n    - name: Encode\n      signature: \"func Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error\"\n    - name: Decode\n      signature: \"func Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error\"\n    - name: OpenInput\n      signature: \"func OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error)\"\n  imports:\n    - io\n    - os\n    - bufio\n    - strings\n  import_constraints:\n    - \"Must not import any cmd/ package.\"\n    - \"Must not import any other pkg/ package.\"\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"Encode with Base64 encoder wraps at 76 characters by default.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"Encode with WrapCol=0 produces single-line output.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Decode with Base64 decoder and IgnoreGarbage=true ignores non-alphabet characters.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Decode with IgnoreGarbage=false returns error on invalid input.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"OpenInput('-') returns os.Stdin.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"pkg/encutil compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n","numLines":121,"startLine":1,"totalLines":121}}}
