{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed stitch task (#5097) for the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement srd088-encutil requirements R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2 by replacing the `panic(\"not implemented\")` stubs in `pkg/encutil/decode.go` with working implementations of the `Decode` and `OpenInput` functions. The task is part of an automated code generation pipeline (cobbler-scaffold), and git is managed externally — no git commands should be run.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - srd088-encutil: Shared encoding/decoding library for base32, base64, basenc utilities\n   - DecoderConfig struct with `Decode func(string) ([]byte, error)` and `IgnoreGarbage bool`\n   - Generic decode pipeline that strips whitespace and optionally strips non-alphabet garbage characters\n   - OpenInput pattern returning os.Stdin for \"-\" or \"\" filename\n   - Superset encoding alphabet for garbage filtering (A-Za-z0-9+/=-_) covering Base64, Base64URL, Base32, Base32hex, Base16\n   - Import constraints: must not import any cmd/ or other pkg/ package\n   - Differential testing pattern used across the project\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines hard limit\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd088-encutil.yaml` (READ)\n     - Read to understand exact requirements R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2\n     - Key requirements: Decode strips whitespace always, strips non-alphabet chars when IgnoreGarbage=true, returns error on invalid chars when IgnoreGarbage=false; OpenInput returns os.Stdin for \"\" or \"-\"\n   \n   - `pkg/encutil/decode.go` (READ then MODIFIED)\n     - Original had panic stubs for Decode and OpenInput\n     - Replaced with full implementations\n     - Final written content:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n     package encutil\n\n     import (\n         \"io\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n     )\n\n     type DecoderConfig struct {\n         Decode        func(string) ([]byte, error)\n         IgnoreGarbage bool\n     }\n\n     func Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error {\n         data, err := io.ReadAll(r)\n         if err != nil {\n             return err\n         }\n         input := stripWhitespace(string(data))\n         if cfg.IgnoreGarbage {\n             input = stripGarbage(input)\n         }\n         decoded, err := cfg.Decode(input)\n         if err != nil {\n             return err\n         }\n         _, err = w.Write(decoded)\n         return err\n     }\n\n     func stripWhitespace(s string) string {\n         var b strings.Builder\n         b.Grow(len(s))\n         for i := 0; i < len(s); i++ {\n             ch := s[i]\n             if ch != ' ' && ch != '\\t' && ch != '\\n' && ch != '\\r' {\n                 b.WriteByte(ch)\n             }\n         }\n         return b.String()\n     }\n\n     func stripGarbage(s string) string {\n         var b strings.Builder\n         b.Grow(len(s))\n         for i := 0; i < len(s); i++ {\n             if isEncodingAlphabet(s[i]) {\n                 b.WriteByte(s[i])\n             }\n         }\n         return b.String()\n     }\n\n     func isEncodingAlphabet(ch byte) bool {\n         return (ch >= 'A' && ch <= 'Z') ||\n             (ch >= 'a' && ch <= 'z') ||\n             (ch >= '0' && ch <= '9') ||\n             ch == '+' || ch == '/' || ch == '=' ||\n             ch == '-' || ch == '_'\n     }\n\n     func OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error) {\n         if filename == \"\" || filename == \"-\" {\n             return os.Stdin, nil\n         }\n         return os.Open(filename)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/encutil/encode.go` (provided in context, not modified)\n     - Reference for consistent style patterns (Encode function, writeWrapped helper)\n     - Contains EncoderConfig struct and Encode function implementation\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Write tool error \"File has not been read yet\"**: \n     - Attempted to Write `pkg/encutil/decode.go` before Reading it\n     - Fixed by first calling Read on the file, then calling Write with the full implementation\n     - No user feedback on this - it was a tool constraint error\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved the key design problem of how to handle garbage stripping generically without knowing the specific encoding alphabet. Decided to use a superset alphabet (A-Za-z0-9+/=-_) that covers all common base encodings (Base64, Base64URL, Base32, Base32hex, Base16).\n   - The approach: always strip whitespace, conditionally strip non-superset-alphabet chars when IgnoreGarbage=true, then pass to caller's Decode function.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task prompt containing the full project context, SRDs, source code, execution constitution, go style constitution, task description, requirements, design decisions, acceptance criteria, and constraints. The core request is to implement srd088-encutil R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2 in `pkg/encutil/decode.go`.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Run `go build ./pkg/encutil/...` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./pkg/encutil/...` to verify no issues (AC2)\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria AC1-AC5 are satisfied\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was in the middle of implementing task #5097 - replacing panic stubs in `pkg/encutil/decode.go` with full implementations of `Decode` and `OpenInput`. The file has been successfully written with the implementations. The next step per the task instructions is to verify the code compiles and passes checks:\n   \n   From the task: \"4. **Verify** — Check every item in Acceptance Criteria. Run tests if the criteria require it. Do not skip any criterion.\"\n   \n   Acceptance criteria that still need verification:\n   - AC1: \"go build ./pkg/encutil/... succeeds\"\n   - AC2: \"go vet ./pkg/encutil/... reports no issues\"\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Run `go build ./pkg/encutil/...` and `go vet ./pkg/encutil/...` to verify the implementation compiles and has no issues, completing acceptance criteria AC1 and AC2. This is directly required by the task's step 4: \"**Verify** — Check every item in Acceptance Criteria. Run tests if the criteria require it. Do not skip any criterion.\" The working directory is `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5097`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5097/4fc28f23-4d8c-4641-908e-5e9d69890c03.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4fc28f23-4d8c-4641-908e-5e9d69890c03","uuid":"d83a2c3b-2c33-49fa-ae7f-437086662e49","timestamp":"2026-05-13T23:47:48.492Z","isSynthetic":true}
